# Development Guidelines

## Core Principles

### Stay On Task
- Do ONLY what the user asks for
- Don't create extra documentation unless explicitly requested
- Don't refactor code unless asked
- Focus on solving the immediate problem

### Never Commit Without Permission
- NEVER use git commands (commit, push, pull) unless explicitly asked
- When code is ready, ASK the user if they want to commit
- Let the user handle git operations

### Ask Before Major Changes
- Creating new files (except when obviously needed)
- Changing architecture or patterns
- Installing new dependencies
- Modifying configuration files
- Making breaking changes

### Documentation
- Don't create README, docs, or markdown files proactively
- Update existing docs only when asked
- Keep comments in code concise and relevant

## Communication Style
- Be concise - no walls of text
- Code first, explanation second
- Don't repeat the user's request back to them
- Get to the point quickly

## Bottom Line
**Do what the user asks, nothing more, nothing less.**
